# Outcome

Although the model did not consistently invoke the registered tools due to the interaction between Retrieval-Augmented Generation and model behavior, this phase provided a strong understanding of how Tool Calling works within LangChain4j.

More importantly, it demonstrated that building AI systems involves more than exposing functionality—it requires careful consideration of model capabilities, prompting, and overall application architecture.

This knowledge forms the foundation for more advanced agent architectures in future phases.
